                  },
                  "linkStyle": {
                    "inherit": true,
                    "linkColor": "#514293",
                    "linkHoverColor": "#514293",
                    "linkUnderline": true,
                    "linkHoverUnderline": true
                  },
                  "text": "<strong>3</strong> &nbsp; Product Designer Rogie King was on a mission to bring shaders to Figma—but first, he had to assemble the right team. Here’s what it took to ship these generative tools: an airtight pitch, a prototype-first process, and <strong><u>a passion that was contagious.</u></strong>",
                  "fontSize": "16px",
                  "fontFamily": {
                    "label": "Arial",
                    "value": "arial,helvetica,sans-serif"
